{
  "$comment": "US GENIUS covenant — positive controls for config/genius-wall-patterns.json, read by BOTH walls (apps/web genius-stablecoin-wall.test.ts and the apps/sandbox mirror in messages.test.ts). Every concrete form the patterns name is listed, and each earn and earnNear form is tested in three positions ('USDC <form>.', '<form>: USDC', '(<form>) USDC'), so narrowing an alternative's boundary at either side fails both walls. Each stable form is tested with 'earns'; each earn form with 'USDC'; 'breaches' are whole sentences found in reviews. Lists may only GROW (each has a floor in the tests). Fifth audit 2026-11-05: the first controls pinned one form per alternative, and 'digital(?:en)?' or 'rende' alone passed every test. Sixth audit 2026-11-05: the controls were whole words while the patterns match word STARTS, so cutting endings ('earn(?!ed|ing)', 'dollar\\\\b', 'USDC\\\\b') stayed green; every inflection is now listed, the 40-character window is pinned by a generated control at exactly windowChars past the 40th character, the case flag by an all-caps breach, and duplicates are refused. 2026-11-17 (register 5.811, 5.958, plan P9): the floors alone never stopped a control from being REPLACED by a string that still pairs through another word ('wuchs' rewritten as 'rendeu wuchs' kept the count), so scripts/check-genius-controls-grow.mjs, run in CI's quality job, fails when any entry of stableForms, earnForms, rateForms, earnNearForms or breaches disappears against the pull request's base, or windowChars shrinks. rateForms are notations only; the walls put '5%', '5% ' and '5 % ' before each. Every earn form and every rate notation must also match earn ALONE, with no window, because GENIUS-COMBO-1 reads earn only; a multi-word earn form without a digit is also tested across a line break. earnNearForms must pair inside the window AND must not match earn alone (D2). nonEarnForms are look-alikes the windowless earn must never match, and the ones that are not growth nouns must not match earnNear either (D4): a ceiling, removed only by a founder ruling (the CI step warns, it does not block); a failing entry means reword the copy or ask the founder to rule, never narrow the pattern.",
